  "display_name": "Ultra-basic models: every aircraft, vehicle, site and building as a few primitives",
  "status": "First pass, 18 October 2026 (docs/scenery/README.md). Placeholders until real models exist: the right size, a recognisable silhouette, a colour per side.",
  "source": "game value: placeholders built from primitives; overall length, span and height are approximate public dimensions of each type, for scale only (presentation data, like data/cabins/)",
  "confidence": "estimate",
  "notes": "Each model is an archetype with a few parameters; simcore/scenery/basic_models.hpp expands it into parts (box, cylinder, cone, sphere) in the model's frame: x forward, y right, z up, metres, the origin on the ground under the middle (aircraft: at the middle of the fuselage). Archetypes: jet (length, span, height, engines, wing swept/delta/straight/variable, tail conventional/twin/none), prop (biplane, high_wing), helicopter (rotor_m, wings), drone, missile (diameter_m), wheeled (axles, turret, radar dish/bar/none, missiles, mast, cab), tracked (turret, gun, radar, missiles), truck (body cargo/tank/box), launcher (rails, missile_m, elevation_deg), gun (barrels), building (roof pitched/flat), church, tower (diameter_m: chimneys, cooling towers, tanks), tent, mast, tree (crown cone/round), bridge, crates. Colours are names from 'colours' or #rrggbb. The aircraft models carry the air war's aircraft ids (data/air_war/faction_*.json): test_scenery checks every one has a model.",
